Remove only the PE_kputc takeover that zzz-boot-progress.patch adds in PE_init_kprintf().
With it in place early kprintf bypasses the console buffer, so the USB CDC ring is never fed
and the serial channel goes silent once the progress page binds (measured as L103). The two
page hooks in serial_console.c and video_console.c stay, so the page still draws while
console output keeps flowing to the ring.

--- a/pexpert/arm/pe_kprintf.c
+++ b/pexpert/arm/pe_kprintf.c
@@ -86,7 +86,6 @@
 static void
 PE_init_kprintf(void)
 {
-	if (boot_progress_active()) { PE_kputc = boot_progress_putc; return; }
 	if (serial_init()) {
 		PE_kputc = serial_putc_crlf;
 	} else {
